 Welcome, this little converter was written so that I could convert the
 new 8 bitplane Iff pictures that became available with the AGA/AA chip
 set found in the A1200 and A4000 computers. 
      This new version features two new commands and a new command line
 reader making it easier both for me and for you to use.


  Available options :-
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

    B - Place the colour map behind the binary image you have saved.
	< default is before >

    C - Cancel Saving colours. < default saves >

    F - Save the colurs as a separate file. < default saves to binary file >

    H - Instructs the program this is a HAM8 image for saving.
	< default normal IFF image >

    S - Change output file to sequential data. < default interleaved >

    T - Select old 12 bit colour values. < default 24 bit >
	

  If no options are selected then the defaults will be used.


 Additional Information
 «====================»

	If when saving the colours there are more than 32 ie new chipset
  screen mode 64, 128 or 256 colours and they are the 24 bit size values,
  they are arranged in the following format.

   For example an Iff 128 colour image:-



   First a bank of 128 words in the following order.

   Colour Range   0 - 31, 32 - 63, 64 - 95, 96 - 127. Bits $ f0 f0 f0



   Then a second bank of 128 words in the following order.

   Colour Range   0 - 31, 32 - 63, 64 - 95, 96 - 127. Bits $ 0f 0f 0f



   Compatability
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	This converter should be compatible on all Amigas regardless
   of memory, chipset type or kickstart version.











